WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.220
Stand at the top of a deep, dry well.

2
00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:04.900
Let go of a stone.

3
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:09.440
With air resistance negligible,
gravity is the only force acting.

4
00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:12.440
Its acceleration is
constant: the same size,

5
00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.420
always downwards, whatever its mass.

6
00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:19.420
After 1 second, it has fallen
a distance we'll call d.

7
00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.690
How far does it fall in the next second?

8
00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.770
The same again?

9
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:23.930
Twice as far?

10
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:24.980
More?

11
00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:28.980
In this mission, you'll meet the equations
that link five quantities whenever

12
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.020
acceleration is constant.

13
00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.630
Then you'll follow a
ball thrown straight up,

14
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:36.630
and find out what is
happening at the very top.

15
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.720
Your mission: predict how far the
stone falls in the next second,

16
00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:41.800
in terms of d.
